 lowering rule used the height **before**\n1621\t  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n1622\t  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n1623\t- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n1624\t  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n1625\t  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n1626\t  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n1627\t  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n1628\t  partition the stack (item 9).\n1629\t- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n1630\t  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n1631\t  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n1632\t  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n1633\t  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n1634\t- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n1635\t- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n1636\t  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n1637\t  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n1638\t  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n1639\t  exists. **Amended after 6b (2026-10-13):** 4b stage 2 landed before\n1640\t  6b, and rows 3-4, 7-12, 17 and 24 now run on the reference lane (89\n1641\t  labelled row × segment executions, 85 distinct builder/wrapper setups\n1642\t  since rows 3 and 24 share one builder by design); rows 10-11 were\n1643\t  re-read and corrected (§5.2, B1). The 6b harness ran on the JVM only;\n1644\t  Node and Dart execution of `rows.cljc`'s transport and the new harness\n1645\t  file remain the three-host gate of §8.2 item 9, not established by the\n1646\t  reviews.\n1647\t\n1648\t---\n1649\t\n1650\t## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n1651\t\n1652\