urce-index` held for it\n1713\t(derivations design §9.2).\" **Replace `:513-527`** (\"Loading a fetched\n1714\tvector has two paths … nothing may depend on which path a conforming\n1715\tengine takes.\") with: \"Loading a fetched vector has **one path**: the\n1716\tdirect decode of the canonical vector into an image through the one\n1717\tvalidator (`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). The projection\n1718\tpath (vector → datoms → loader) is retired (owner ruling 2026-09-18;\n1719\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4). The conformance obligation is\n1720\tthat the two AST projection lanes and the direct vector load yield one\n1721\timage and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`).\"\n1722\t\n1723\t**U2 — §7.4.1 (ACCEPT).** At its head: \"Superseded for the\n1724\tregister-shaped machine by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.1 (two\n1725\tstate columns, `act` and `tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table\n1726\tbelow describes the stack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's\n1727\tphase 8.\" Replace the `:yin.k/frame` example with §1.2's keyed form.\n1728\t\n1729\t**U3 — §7.4.2 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace, in the opening\n1730\tparagraph, \"absolute stack depth and environment key sets at a pc depend\n1731\ton the *activation* — a closure enters with the caller's residual\n1732\toperand stack and an environment formed from its captured environment\n1733\tplus arguments (`apply-call`), and §2.6 enforces no equal stack heights\n1734\tat joins, so the same pc is legitimately reached at many depths\" with\n1735\t\"the saved window's values, the environment's bindings and the depth of\n1736\t`K` at a pc depend on the *activation*; the same pc is legitimately\n1737\treached under many windows and environments\". Replace \"E, St, and every\n1738\tK frame's `:stack-base` and env travel in the value\" with \"E, the saved\n1739\twindow, and every K frame's window, `rd` and env travel in the value, as\n1740\tdoes the task's free environment\". In the static map replace\n1741\t`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]` with `[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}]\n1742\t[sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`; in the\n1743\trules replace \"`stack-effect` and `lexically-required` are derived from\n1744\tthe canonical vector alone, by the same static walk the linearizer\n1745\tperforms (§5.3). They are identical for every engine and checkable\n1746\tagainst the reference machine by a conformance test that runs the\n1747\tsegment to each safepoint and compares the observed deltas and E-reads.\n1748\tAbsolute depth, activation bases, captured environments, and physical\n1749\tlayouts are not claimed\" with \"`def`, `use`, `live` and\n1750\t`lexically-required` are derived from the canonical vector alone\n1751\t(`yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis`). They are identical for every\n1752\tengine and checkable against the reference machine by a conformance test\n1753\tthat runs the segment to each safepoint and compares the saved window's\n1754\tkey set with `live − {rd}` and the E-reads. Window values, environments,\n1755\t`K` and physical layouts are not claimed\"; replace \"physical slot →\n1756\tcanonical slot\" with \"physical location → virtual register\n1757\t(continuation design §4)\".\n1758\t\n1759\t**U4 — §7.4.3 (ACCEPT).** After \"Three rules make these resumable\":\n1760\t\"A pending rides on an `act` state (write-result delivery) or a `tail`\n1761\tstate (through-return delivery); the variants are unchanged, and\n1762\t`:yin.k/registers R` of the version-2 amendment is the `act`/`tail`\n1763\tstate of the frozen design §4.2.\"\n1764\t\n1765\t**U5 — §7.6 (ACCEPT).** In §7.6.1's example add\n1766\t`:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}  ; §7.6.1a` and a new §7.6.1a with\n1767\tthe phase-5 §9.2 UCF row text verbatim, including its completeness\n1768\tclause (absent or empty is incomplete).\n1769\t\n1770\t**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \"Safepoint conformance\n1771\tharness\" replace \"including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the static\n1772\t`stack-effect`/`lexically-required` checks\" with \"including `lift ∘\n1773\tlower = id` on canonical frames, the static `def`/`use`/`live` and\n1774\t`lexically-required` checks, the frame validator on every frame, and\n1775\t**cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint lifts\n1776\tto row sets with equal root ids after the harness's specified\n1777\tre-emission (continuation design §5.5) from the semantic-register kernel\n1778\tand from the stack and register kernels through their layouts, the stack\n1779\tkernel with its tail-completion seam\". In §7.11.1 \"Safepoint\n1780\treconstruction\", replace \"Separately prepare two independently\n1781\timplemented UCF engines\" with \"Separately prepare the three engines\n1782\tintended to reconstruct canonical frames (the semantic-register kernel;\n1783\tthe register kernel; the stack kernel after its tail-completion seam)\"\n1784\tand \"the frame, pending wait, next result, and effect trace must agree\n1785\tin both directions\" with \"the canonical row set after re-emission, the\n1786\tpending wait, next result and effect trace must agree across all three\n1787\tand in every lowering direction\".\n1788\t\n1789\t### 10.3 To the row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`)\n1790\t\n1791\tThe inventory below is every clause the grep of the draft for\n1792\t\"legacy\", \"version 0/1/2\", \"semantic profile only / semantic-only\",\n1793\t\"does not translate\", \"unchanged / do not move\", \"other profile\",\n1794\t\"registry\" found operative; each is replaced or deleted.\n1795\t\n1796\t**R1 — §2 `:50-81` (ACCEPT).** Replace the section with: \"**Body\n1797\tversion 3, one profile.** The carrier is body version 3 and reads no\n1798\tother version (owner, 2026-10-11: no legacy): a body of version 0, 1 or\n1799\t2 is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` at the gate and is never normalised or\n1800\tupgraded. The profile map is `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`;\n18