te reads decoded task\n1832\tcontext, never an engine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the\n1833\ttask's live `:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n1834\t`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\n1835\tsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n1836\t`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\"\n1837\t\n1838\t**R5 — §5.5 `:383-401` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the root with\n1839\tcontinuation §2.6 (adds `free-env-cref`; `contract` is the one profile\n1840\tmap; `code` is `{A \"v4\"-vector}`; `requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`); in\n1841\t`:394` replace \"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map, unchanged`\" with\n1842\t\"`requires ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees`\".\n1843\t\n1844\t**R6 — §8 step 7 `:661-667` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace with:\n1845\t\"**Frames.** Every `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and\n1846\tparked-table state is decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n1847\t`yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n1848\t`:captured`, `:parked`) and the decoded task context (parked key, live\n1849\tFFI call ids, the root's free environment); a defect is\n1850\t`:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path (continuation\n1851\t§3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6) and before\n1852\tpending validation (step 8).\"\n1853\t\n1854\t**R6a — §8 step 1 `:618-623`.** Replace \"then every profile map against\n1855\tthe registry (only the semantic profile is supported, §2)\" with \"then\n1856\tevery profile map against the one profile map of §2\".\n1857\t\n1858\t**R7 — `:63-68` and §10.4 `:774-777` (ACCEPT).** Delete \"Code stamps\n1859\t`\"v3\"`, `\"b2\"`, `\"r2\"` and the inner version 1 do not move: this is a\n1860\tchange of carrier, not of instruction, scheduler, or value semantics,\n1861\texactly the distinction the amendment draws between its versions and\n1862\texecutable code.\" Replace §10.4 with: \"**Contract stamp.** The code\n1863\tcontract carried is `\"v4\"`, the register-shaped machine's; the carrier\n1864\tversion is 3; the two are independent, and neither names a legacy\n1865\tvalue.\"\n1866\t\n1867\t**R8 — §9 `:737-746` \"Legacy correspondence\" and §10.8 `:797-801`\n1868\t(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Delete both: there is no legacy reader and no\n1869\tnormalisation tool. In §10.3 `:769-773` delete \"Versions 0, 1 and 2\n1870\tremain compatibility inputs. One canonical nested projection of version\n1871\t3 is kept for single-message channels and must stay exactly mutually\n1872\tinverse with the rows.\" and \"Retiring old readers is an owner\n1873\tversion-support decision\", leaving \"Rows are the carrier authority.\"\n1874\tIn §9's law list delete \"Exact mutual inversion is required only between\n1875\tversion 3 and its one canonical nested projection (§10.3)\".\n1876\t\n1877\t**R9 — §10.6 `:782-788`, §10.7 `:792-796`, §2 `:70-81`, §10's\n1878\tproposals list `:821-834`, \"Still open\" `:836-837`, §11 `:839-852`\n1879\t(ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** §10.6, **whole item**: replace its opening\n1880\t\"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before any implementation\n1881\tbrief claims heterogeneous execution conformance, and not drafted here\"\n1882\twith \"**Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an\n1883\timplementation brief claims execution conformance for an engine\n1884\t**outside the three repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and\n1885\tthe stack and register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n1886\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\n1887\tprofile), and not drafted here\"; keep its list of what such a profile\n1888\tmust cover; and replace \"version 3, like version 2, does\n1889\tnot translate between kernels\" with \"version 3 carries the canonical\n1890\tframe; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through its layout\n1891\t(continuation §4), which is